    "id": "catalog.L188.8",
    "class": "equivalent",
    "justification": "In audit() the str branch starts at module_utils/connectome_catalog.py:187, and the original condition of line 188 (value != '/') is false for exactly one string, the single character '/'. For that string the mutated code falls through to the next refusal with the same text: line 189 passes because the value holds no file:// prefix, line 190 leaves it unchanged, line 191 passes because it holds no file: text, line 192 removes no URL, the ABSOLUTE pattern of line 176 matches the whole string in the loop of line 193, line 194 strips it to the empty string, and line 195 need(bool(raw), 'root dependency refused') raises ArchiveError with the same message and the same code E_CATALOG_INVALID that line 188 raised. Nothing between lines 188 and 195 does IO or changes state. For every other string line 188 passes in both versions. Kill attempts before waiving: '/' as a value, as a mapping key, as a list element and nested were each run against the original and the mutated module and gave identical exception class, message, code and args; near misses such as a doubled slash or a slash with surrounding spaces do not make the original condition false, so they cannot tell the versions apart either.",
    "no_observable_difference": "Every input of audit(): non-string values never reach line 188; every string other than '/' satisfies the original condition, so both versions run the same code; the string '/' is refused in both versions with ArchiveError('root dependency refused', code E_CATALOG_INVALID) and no side effect. Only the traceback line (188 or 195) differs. The argument assumes the built-in str comparison and methods, which holds for everything JSON, YAML, argv or a file can supply; an object that overrides its own inequality operator is outside it.",
