    "id": "catalog.L537.8",
    "class": "unreachable",
    "justification": "module_utils/connectome_catalog.py:537 need(bool(argv), 'empty launcher command') can never see a falsy argv. Line 530 strips each launcher line with str.strip() and line 534 skips it when it is empty or starts with '#', so line 536 calls literal_words on a string whose first character is not whitespace. literal_words (lines 477-483) either raises, on line 478 for a refused character or on line 483 when shlex.split raises ValueError for an unterminated quote (need(False, ...) always raises, so the function never returns None), or it returns shlex.split(value). shlex.split runs a POSIX lexer with whitespace_split set and no comment characters. Its whitespace set (space, tab, carriage return, line feed) is a subset of what str.strip removed, so the first character opens a word or a quoted section; the lexer emits a token for every opened word and for every closed quote (an empty quoted string yields the empty token), and the escape character that could swallow a character is refused on line 478. The returned list therefore has at least one element whenever line 537 runs. Kill attempts before waiving: a line of only quotes (it yields one empty word and is refused later by audit_argv as 'command must be nonempty argv' in both versions), lines of exotic whitespace and control characters, and a brute force over every one- and two-character line from U+0000 to U+00FF plus U+0085, U+00A0, U+2028 and U+3000, and every line of up to four characters from a quote, whitespace and control alphabet: none makes literal_words return an empty list.",
    "no_observable_difference": "Every launcher body passed to audit_launcher (any str): the condition on line 537 is true each time it is evaluated, so both versions return the same list of working directories or raise the same ArchiveError with the same message and code.",
    "area": "catalog_b",
    "anchor": {
      "file": "module_utils/connectome_catalog.py",
      "line": 537,
      "before": "bool(argv)",
      "after": "True"
    }
  },
