    "class": "unreachable",
    "justification": "module_utils/connectome_catalog.py:679 refuses a preflight word that holds a percent sign, dollar sign, line feed, carriage return, backslash or double quote. It is dominated by audit_argv on line 676, which preflight_unit calls without data_args. audit_argv requires every word to be a non-empty str (line 233). The executable goes through audit_path (line 237), whose line 205 requires a full match of [A-Za-z0-9_.+@/-]+. Every later word is exactly '--' (line 241), or an option without '=' that fully matches --[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9-]*|-[A-Za-z0-9] (lines 246 and 249-250), or such an option followed by '=' and a value that goes through audit_path (lines 256-258; the data_args branch on line 252 is dead because the mapping is empty), or a plain word that goes through audit_path (line 258). A word that audit_argv accepts is therefore built only from letters, digits and the characters _ . + @ / = and -, none of which line 679 refuses, so its condition is true whenever it is evaluated. Kill attempts before waiving: option values, words after '--', attached short options and words ending in a line feed (a full match does not tolerate a trailing line feed); an exhaustive run over every word of up to four characters from an alphabet that includes the six refused characters, placed as executable, operand, operand after '--', long-option value and short option, found 6426 accepted argv lists and none that holds a refused character. The same mutation is the site mutant of the named check catalog.preflight.chars, which is recorded as unresolved because names cannot be waived.",
    "no_observable_difference": "Every config whose preflight run words are str objects: a word that holds one of the six characters is already refused inside audit_argv on line 676, before line 679 runs, so preflight_unit returns the same unit text or raises the same ArchiveError in both versions. Only a str subclass that misreports its own contents could differ, and no JSON or YAML input produces one.",
